  <conversation ID="Barathrum">
    <start>
      <choice ID="Vixy_TeachModLegendary" Target="Vixy_TaughtModLegendary" Ordinal="9700">
        <text>Master, teach me to make something that outlasts me.</text>
        <part Name="Vixy_TeachLegendary" />
      </choice>
    </start>
    <node ID="Vixy_TaughtModLegendary">
      <text
      >Masterwork is a thing made well. Legendary is a thing made once. The difference is not in the steel, child - it is in refusing to set it down.</text>
      <choice Target="Start">
        <text>Thank you, =pronouns.formalAddressTerm=.</text>
      </choice>
    </node>
  </conversation>

  <!-- Bep teaches microserrated. #723.

       One teacher per recipe, so a tinker is a person worth finding rather than one of four
